## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical guardrails for real-world, globally distributed Azure workloads, focusing on logs/telemetry leakage, secret rotation, and safe rollback.

## Key Concepts

- Managed Identities with least privilege RBAC
- Key Vault references over inline secrets
- Azure Policy gates (no secrets in env vars/connection strings)
- Application Insights masking and diagnostic redaction
- Canary deployments with telemetry-driven rollback

## Code Example

```javascript
// Node.js example: fetch secret via DefaultAzureCredential and KeyVaultSecretClient
const { DefaultAzureCredential } = require('@azure/identity');
const { SecretClient } = require('@azure/keyvault-secrets');
const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
const client = new SecretClient("https://<kv-name>.vault.azure.net/", credential);
async function getSecret(name) {
  const secret = await client.getSecret(name);
  return secret.value;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the guardrail during a canary rollout?
- What logging changes would you implement to ensure no secrets are emitted even in error traces?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical CMK usage, Key Vault integration, identity access, policy enforcement, and rollback planning at beginner level.

## Key Concepts
- Customer-managed keys (CMK) for storage at rest
- Azure Key Vault with managed identities
- Storage Account encryption properties and keyVaultProperties
- Azure Policy to require CMK on new storage accounts
- Canary rollout and rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// ARM-like snippet illustrating CMK encryption on a storage account
{
  "type": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts",
  "name": "[storageAccountName]",
  "apiVersion": "2023-01-01",
  "location": "[resourceGroup().location]",
  "properties": {
    "encryption": {
      "keySource": "Microsoft.KeyVault",
      "keyVaultProperties": {
        "keyName": "<cmk-name>",
        "keyVaultUri": "https://<vault-name>.vault.azure.net/"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate CMK policy compliance in CI/CD? 
- How would you handle CMK rotation without downtime?

## Why This Is Asked
Assess hands-on orchestration across Azure components during incidents, focusing on tenant isolation, automated rollback safety, and auditable controls.

## Key Concepts
- UEBA-driven automation (Defender for Cloud/Sentinel)
- Per-tenant network isolation (NSG, Private Endpoint)
- Key Vault key rotation and re-encryption
- Token revocation and Conditional Access control
- Canary-based rollback mechanisms
- Centralized auditing and alerting

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo orchestrator snippet
async function quarantineTenant(tenantId){
  await applyPerTenantNSG(tenantId);
  await rotateKeyVaultKeys(tenantId);
  await revokeTokensAndDisableCA(tenantId);
  await rollbackToLastGoodRelease(tenantId);
}
```
